member.summary:
Concatenates property values from a collection using the specified selector. 
If all the values are the same, returns the first property value; 
otherwise, returns the concatenated string of all property values.

member.example:
Example usage:

int[] numbers = { 1, 2, 3 };
string result = ToDelimitedString(numbers, ","); // Output: "1,2,3"

member.returns:
A new string in which all literal occurrences of  in 
are replaced with , ignoring case;
or the original string if no matches are found.

member.param:
When this method returns, contains the parsed integer value if successful;
otherwise, the default value for  if  is true and key not found,
or the result of parsing if present.

When this method returns, contains the parsed double value if successful;
otherwise, the default value for  if  is true and key not found,
or the result of parsing if present.

member.summary:

Calculate V_DP_K =  ((V_1 I_2-V_2 I_1 ) R_term)/(V_1-V_2+(R_term-R_(path) )(I_2-I_1 ) ), where R_term = 45ohm; Rpath = trace + RAK
Alg::TX_Level(ed_j15_1, ed_j15_2,0.0001,0.001,ATC0_USB_ED_P,40[,edp_j15]);
Alg::TX_Level(ed_j15_1, ed_j15_2,0.0001,0.001,ATC0_USB_ED_N,40[,edp_j15,vdiff_15mv_p1]);

