member.remarks:
The method uses the assignment string as a template and replaces the sweep source names with their corresponding bit patterns, 
generating all possible combinations of the bit patterns.


string assignment = "DigSrcA=sweep1;DigSrcB=sweep2";
string customerString = "sweepsrc:sweep1=000,001,010;sweep2=100,101,110";

SweepCondition sweepCondition = SweepAlgorithm.ProcessSweepString(customerString);
sweepCondition.SetupDigSrcAssignment(assignment);
string[] sweepSrcArray = sweepCondition.GetSweepArray();

sweepSrcArray will contain:
"DigSrcA=000;DigSrcB=100", "DigSrcA=000;DigSrcB=101", "DigSrcA=000;DigSrcB=110",
"DigSrcA=001;DigSrcB=100", "DigSrcA=001;DigSrcB=101", "DigSrcA=001;DigSrcB=110",
"DigSrcA=010;DigSrcB=100", "DigSrcA=010;DigSrcB=101", "DigSrcA=010;DigSrcB=110"

The method evaluates the values associated with the given codes and determines the best code
based on the criteria set by the TrimTargetPosition: Above, Closest, and Below.

Example scenarios:
-------------------------------------------------- 
- If the next value is NaN:
Value=  {   N/A,    +0.1,   N/A,    N/A     }
Code=   {   0,      1,      2,      3       }
Curr=   {    ,      V,       ,              }
Next=   {    ,       ,      V,              }
[All]       IsFind= false, BestCode= N/A, BestValue= N/A.
Value=  {   N/A,    N/A,    -0.1,   N/A     }
Code=   {   0,      1,      2,      3       }
Curr=   {    ,       ,      V,              }
Next=   {    ,      V,       ,              }
[All]       IsFind= false, BestCode= N/A, BestValue= N/A.
--------------------------------------------------
- If the current value is positive and the next value is negative:
Value=  {   +0.2,   +0.1,   -0.1,   -0.2    }
Code=   {   0,      1,      2,      3       }
Curr=   {    ,      V,       ,              }
Next=   {    ,       ,      V,              }
[Above]     IsFind= true, BestCode= 2, BestValue= -0.1. (Choose Next)
[Closest]   IsFind= true, BestCode= 1, BestValue= +0.1. (Choose Min or Curr)
[Below]     IsFind= true, BestCode= 1, BestValue= +0.1. (Choose Curr)
--------------------------------------------------
- If the current value is negative and the next value is positive:
Value=  {   +0.2,   +0.1,   -0.1,   -0.2    }
Code=   {   0,      1,      2,      3       }
Curr=   {    ,       ,      V,              }
Next=   {    ,      V,       ,              }
[Above]     IsFind= true, BestCode= 2, BestValue= -0.1. (Choose Curr)
[Closest]   IsFind= true, BestCode= 2, BestValue= -0.1. (Choose Min or Curr)
[Below]     IsFind= true, BestCode= 1, BestValue= +0.1. (Choose Next)
--------------------------------------------------
- If the current value is equal to the next value:
Value=  {   +0.4,   +0.3,   +0.2,   +0.1    }
Code=   {   0,      1,      2,      3       }
Curr=   {    ,       ,       ,      V       }
Next=   {    ,       ,       ,      V       }
[All]       IsFind= true, BestCode= 3, BestValue= +0.1. (Choose Curr)
Value=  {   -0.1,   -0.2,   -0.3,   -0.4    }
Code=   {   0,      1,      2,      3       }
Curr=   {   V,       ,       ,              }
Next=   {   V,       ,       ,              }
[All]       IsFind= true, BestCode= 0, BestValue= -0.1. (Choose Curr)
--------------------------------------------------

